n the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=1$ and $Q(x,y)=x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}dx+x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\pi -\\pi  \\\\  & =3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369434 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fe866fa-6339-5f10-8ce3-3d5938c3785e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369436} {:answer/id #uuid "0aafa5fa-6806-5c1a-bd6e-a8f0ec680d0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369437} {:answer/id #uuid "b169f03c-00d2-5df3-887b-9ea86b4a1f34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369438} {:answer/id #uuid "2e03cd88-a4dd-5d49-b397-096aeb5b4219" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369439} {:answer/id #uuid "8e91bdb9-02ae-5c29-aa67-a875b2bc2112" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e03cd88-a4dd-5d49-b397-096aeb5b4219" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369439} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2ee2d3e-bbe0-5737-8885-1738f355a09b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "32a18b85-d978-5b18-8fff-914bdccf82dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-126853" :question/problem "![](images/39/393bed476f2e8d84fc7e5dc721d77749f7f259834e03a94a48a08533ae9befa6.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}2y\\,dx+4x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the region shown above." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=2y$ and $Q(x,y)=4x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}2y\\,dx+4x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4-2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (6\\cdot 4-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (24-4) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 20 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369441 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "992dce16-160e-53f6-8630-c0af64cae1cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369443} {:answer/id #uuid "2bfd9130-7a02-5b45-a0d5-85f79505dd79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369444} {:answer/id #uuid "2ce07f1c-821c-51aa-8553-62af6bab118d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369445} {:answer/id #uuid "905e612c-8067-5089-bf8b-dc0ca7481414" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369446} {:answer/id #uuid "bae5a3fa-eb19-574d-b4eb-7f975d579bd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bfd9130-7a02-5b45-a0d5-85f79505dd79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369444} :answer-field/id #uuid "37fee2c5-b026-5dca-a84d-1a957d12aae4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7aa45530-2cd6-5788-83f4-81c4c36b6f4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-126856" :question/problem "![](images/6b/6b52e4f2f37d6ba6971fbc8f6e1d610ab7e0c9d11341ea3b6a6772bff8f40e37.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}3y\\,dx+2x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=3y$ and $Q(x,y)=2x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}3y\\,dx+2x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2-3)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-1\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =-(\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}) \\\\  & =-(9\\pi -\\pi ) \\\\  & =-8\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74b43056-e8dd-536d-b56a-12ac2800c12b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "364" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369457} {:answer/id #uuid "ca09836f-3c6e-5b5f-841d-68ede18363c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "215" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369458} {:answer/id #uuid "ac3caf47-5329-54b1-8c87-bcf0da3ef96b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "424" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369459} {:answer/id #uuid "b9b5b1dc-7bc7-5bb9-8b23-063bc496f471" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "342" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369460} {:answer/id #uuid "1d2e77d0-1779-5c5c-9e64-d3cabd705415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "124" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74b43056-e8dd-536d-b56a-12ac2800c12b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "364" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369457} :answer-field/id #uuid "175c17d1-364f-5ab7-a6b1-2ce4de237b97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "017f8f34-6e37-562a-87cf-df5a06a7e434" :question/math-academy-id "q-126860" :question/problem "![](images/b5/b5a42039e2501a3909062fd6ed92e0879df03f58fa85a62b5e738e8abc78b903.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}8x\\,dy-5y\\,dx,$ where $D$ is the region shown above." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-5y$ and $Q(x,y)=8x.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-5,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}8x\\,dy-5y\\,dx & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(8-(-5))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}13\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =13{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =13\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =13\\cdot ({8}^{2}-{6}^{2}) \\\\  & =13\\cdot (64-36) \\\\  & =13\\cdot 28 \\\\  & =364.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369497 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e6750b8-75e8-5604-bdf3-5b26e689ff79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369499} {:answer/id #uuid "71c2554d-1b8f-50ee-904e-bf572ea954dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369500} {:answer/id #uuid "d3d1e293-45b2-553f-8738-81af539d167d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369501} {:answer/id #uuid "808c516e-8fb0-5d9d-b3c3-71bd5e0c0d18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369502} {:answer/id #uuid "56bd1130-5922-503b-9779-186620077dd1"