\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441618 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4b95dc2-7fee-5f7c-b4ec-8675b76cbf4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441601} {:answer/id #uuid "c1ef271c-da7e-55bf-8af4-8d0b76cc331e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441603} {:answer/id #uuid "d98c6427-b31b-5669-b745-810c5329aad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441605} {:answer/id #uuid "f4bbcaca-d001-596d-9fe9-529dd184cce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441607} {:answer/id #uuid "fedc8124-d82e-59e9-81de-9b44a8c6f376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441610}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fedc8124-d82e-59e9-81de-9b44a8c6f376" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441610} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c819006-1c8a-567c-839e-c05698400658" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441613}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d4082a24-9ee0-5ed5-bf60-7857736d7c8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-126871" :question/problem "![](images/69/69b42001c8ac5e95e18d89785e73fbba3e78554f9146e59bb50dd618b105f10c.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}4y\\,dx+5x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the region shown above." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=4y$ and $Q(x,y)=5x.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=4,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}4y\\,dx+5x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5-4)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 4}{2}-\\frac{2\\cdot 2}{2} \\\\  & =8-2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498490 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb8d995d-0d7c-54d6-8c3f-aa2cc0e562a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498216} {:answer/id #uuid "ce93c3a1-776f-5631-aafd-89bd7f33c5b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498268} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe50e10-ec80-526e-8c44-4ebed28fb715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498270} {:answer/id #uuid "e1f112d4-518e-59d2-a8ae-9b7896ed80c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498304} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e01110-89b2-522a-b30e-7b877b8b16ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfe50e10-ec80-526e-8c44-4ebed28fb715" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498270} :answer-field/id #uuid "30362ef7-7428-53da-a7f2-7fe7cc3d3d5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09c35a82-4469-5857-aed4-331c374b8ab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-126895" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0db447407835f74476edd20ed5327ff3cc570905f744bbc6c29a66926913ecb5.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}(1-4y)\\,dx+(2+5x)\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=1-4y$ and $Q(x,y)=2+5x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-4,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}dx+x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5-(-4))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}9\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =9\\,\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot 5\\pi  \\\\  & =45\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186519559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0662a46f-bec7-54ca-b240-f60d5d5f1afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518998} {:answer/id #uuid "0e19b2e0-2b38-57c0-b50d-3e99a4fb345c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519013} {:answer/id #uuid "12efe453-d9bc-5e34-bdeb-04e1a1d22aee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519022} {:answer/id #uuid "a0fe6c9c-6868-551d-8a19-e70fb67ab8d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519256} {:answer/id #uuid "d13ea829-20bc-5000-ad9a-b878fad5ad6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0662a46f-bec7-54ca-b240-f60d5d5f1afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518998} :answer-field/id #uuid "69041780-f401-5aab-a5e0-f58cc39dca02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "881df761-fca2-5afa-aea8-d6a6e63a7521" :question/math-academy-id "q-126866" :question/problem "![](images/0f/0f1dd3c66e3bf7d25f286720b360d6af1d6361804ab3ff52835d94f78e5084ee.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}-3y\\,dx+2x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the region shown above." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-3y$ and $Q(x,y)=2x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-3,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}-3y\\,dx+2x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2-(-3))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}5\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =5\\cdot ({4}^{2}-\\frac{2\\cdot 2}{2}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (16-2) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 14 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36c72f44-8cad-59b9-b978-9486a3fb8e1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{51\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538159} {:answer/id #uuid "5035e854-d3a5-5790-9eb6-eb2c68c9a904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538167} {:answer/id #uuid "617c9ac0-970c-54d5-982f-e31ce5878129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{57\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538172} {:answer/id #uuid "6fdec5d1-edeb-5afe-bba5-e721dfcadba9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538176} {:answer/id #uuid "a844d8b0-bab6-5d45-822f-ff3c2b83d953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{51\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a844d8b0-bab6-5d45-822f-ff3c2b83d953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{51\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538191} :answer-field/id #uuid "8546cdef-82e7-5512-88cc-d73209e88c5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0093dc0f-6d13-5136-8a41-4ec719538cf8" :question/problem "![](images/57/573013be1dc56a1ae4d0765b81b8e94006b8402a6da9706b118d43e286fb8291.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}6y\\,dx+9x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=6y$ and $Q(x,y)=9x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=6,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}6y\\,dx+9x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(9-6)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3\\,\\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =3\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}-\\frac{\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{17\\pi}{2}  \\\\  & =\\frac{51\\pi}{2} .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d51d6ac-4c27-54cd-b01f-880b60999800" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "492\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538165} {:answer/id #uuid "55780946-8d44-5da2-bf53-437f89466c35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538169} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba0634d-fd89-51ca-bf2d-52c72119346e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538185} {:answer/id #uuid "a36d97e0-3b01-5109-9dd3-61dfaf2cc216" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "300\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538189} {:answer/id #uuid "b5bd23ab-0096-5f66-92c3-71109a692c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-108\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55780946-8d44-5da2-bf53-437f89466c35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538169} :answer-field/id #uuid "1574ac62-0771-511a-8354-4c35bed7f7ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28489039-fdfa-503c-aed0-769a751abddb" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1e97d150acbe82bf31d0a0e371122ae567d62279b66a5db2a3164180248a5e71.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}-13dx+12x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the annular region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=-13$ and $Q(x,y)=12x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=12.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}-13dx+12x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(12-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}12\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {5}^{2}-\\pi \\cdot {4}^{2}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (25\\pi -16\\pi ) \\\\  & =108\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "338fccf2-f549-585f-af57-a920eb07c34e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-560" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538158} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0eacde-8684-5144-862a-ff9207abd200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-704" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538166} {:answer/id #uuid "ae9d1961-35d2-57dc-9b39-45b4e2119f1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-624" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538194} {:answer/id #uuid "b541b542-9c57-5006-bc4a-4c3a995d3adb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "560" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538196} {:answer/id #uuid "c2f897dc-a433-57f6-aaa4-ca8f6e3515d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-976" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "338fccf2-f549-585f-af57-a920eb07c34e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-560" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538158} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9b981ed-6379-5393-ba8b-72c70879308f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3c303577-d49b-5f6d-ae6a-7c78499f5f3d" :question/problem "![](images/24/245fb5eea54d303236a038f3d1b8253bc6c2e70426bcf0e5f48a40704b47d669.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}9y\\,dx+5x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=9y$ and $Q(x,y)=5x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=9,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}9y\\,dx+5x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5-9)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-4\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-4{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (16\\cdot 12-{4}^{2}-{6}^{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (192-16-36) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 140 \\\\  & =-560.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a326d88-270c-56a5-934b-0ecf38037461" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2016" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538155} {:answer/id #uuid "8ead2f2d-0fbf-581f-a47f-ce631f9f623c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2520" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538182} {:answer/id #uuid "bb86ad3f-4859-534b-a0ba-424359b6630f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2184" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538199} {:answer/id #uuid "c22625c0-8ffa-57ca-b447-c4331e833add" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1960" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538201} {:answer/id #uuid "d0b5dba7-939f-52a8-bc6c-dd82a8901707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1960" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c22625c0-8ffa-57ca-b447-c4331e833add" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1960" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538201} :answer-field/id #uuid "aca3e355-2de5-5a67-a052-93dfcc4e2cf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5c5f644e-f3a9-5505-9151-ceb09a68b40b" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d1b2d83da42a1a95525ce3359e947800af884cd29f1ead6d9dbe4cee1c8dfb40.png)\n\nCalculate ${∮}_{∂D}8y\\,dx-6x\\,dy,$ where $D$ is the region shown above.\n\nThe outer boundary is counterclockwise and each hole boundary is clockwise." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a positively oriented, piecewise-smooth, simple closed curve in the plane, and let $D$ be the region bounded by $C.$ If $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first partial derivatives on an open region containing $D,$ then Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,dx+Q\\,dy={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nGreen's theorem can be extended to include regions containing holes. In such cases, we can apply Green's theorem in the same way as before.\n\nWe have that $P(x,y)=8y$ and $Q(x,y)=-6x.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=8,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}8y\\,dx-6x\\,dy & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-6-8)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-14\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-14{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-14\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =-14\\cdot (16\\cdot 10-{4}^{2}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =-14\\cdot (160-16-4) \\\\  & =-14\\cdot 140 \\\\  & =-1960.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186538181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c67da0d8-518b-5fdb-b6ba-6c1c95c22d9b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Green's Theorem to Regions With Holes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f16cfc2-f619-5e86-9b3b-77f85371764c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-240\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538175} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d7754c-2a5d-5712-9b09-74a2ab844f5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538198} {:answer/id #u